# Test: ze config validate fails on a capability this host cannot provide
# Spec: plan/immediate/spec-kernel-capability-gate.md AC-4
# VALIDATES: the third caller of the one enrolment reaches the same verdict as
# ze doctor and the daemon start, so a config that validates here starts there.
# PREVENTS: the two surfaces disagreeing. A config the operator was told is valid
# and that the daemon then refuses is the worst of both answers.
#
# The verdict is about THIS host. Validating a config written for another machine
# answers about this one, which is why the gate is not inside LoadConfig: that
# loader also runs under offline validation, where a host verdict would be wrong.
# The XFRM kernel capability enrols on Linux ONLY: internal/component/ike/engine/kernelcap_linux.go
# carries the registration behind //go:build linux, because XFRM is a Linux
# dataplane and off Linux ze installs none. So `ze doctor` on darwin emits no
# xfrm diagnostic at all and nothing here can be reached, whatever
# ze.test.kernelcap.xfrm is forced to.
#
# This file passed on darwin until 2026-09-14 only because every stream
# assertion was checked against the whole test's output: its own
# `ze explain <code>` step printed the code its `ze doctor` step was supposed
# to produce. Per-command scoping ended that, and the honest answer is that the
# behaviour is Linux-only.
option=needs-linux

option=env:var=ze.test.kernelcap.xfrm:value=absent

tmpfs=ipsec-capability.conf:terminator=EOF_CONF
vpn {
    ipsec {
        interface lo
        ike-group IKE-1 {
            proposal 1 {
                encryption aes256gcm
                hash sha256
                dh-group 14
            }
        }
        esp-group ESP-1 {
            proposal 1 {
                encryption aes256gcm
            }
        }
        site-to-site {
            peer branch {
                connection-type respond
                remote-address 203.0.113.7
                ike-group IKE-1
                esp-group ESP-1
                authentication {
                    mode pre-shared-secret
                    pre-shared-secret correct-horse-battery-staple
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze config validate ipsec-capability.conf
expect=exit:code=1
expect=stdout:contains=CONFIG_XFRM_USER

# The text rendering prints each error's message; the diagnostic code is the
# structured contract `ze explain <code>` reads, so it is asserted where the
# command emits it, on the json rendering (test/parse/bcrypt-placeholder-rejected.ci).
cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze cli -c "validate config ipsec-capability.conf | json"
expect=exit:code=1
expect=stdout:contains=config-kernel-capability
expect=stdout:contains=CONFIG_XFRM_USER

cmd=foreground:seq=3:exec=ze explain config-kernel-capability
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=refuses to start
